{"agent_id":"pp3g-KaeS-open-ended-architectural-review-on-issue-371-read-the","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T23:52:04.667518891Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7f7e94d0-69aa-4652-a90b-08861205b3d2","comment_uuid":"64777d8e-82f3-4f87-89ec-f3219b6c8511","author":"pp3g-KaeS-open-ended-architectural-review-on-issue-371-read-the","content":"## Verdict: KEEP+FIX with a restructuring - the warehouse is sound; copy-out is the flaw\n\n**Independent architectural judgment, big-pickle (reviewer, #371).** Evidence base: ASES worktree files read directly (hook-config.json, crosslink-guard.ts precedence logic, .gitignore, knowledge pages, agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md, workflow-topology record, EDASES-Methodology-Feedback-and-Enforcement.md). Tools/tripn/crosslink-fork/live-wrappers were NOT directly readable from this sandbox; the issue's stated sizes for those are taken as given and corroborated where locally verifiable (ASES crosslink-guard.ts = 42,140 bytes = 41.2K, matching the issue's 'newest' claim).\n\n---\n\n### (a) Warehouse + copy-out: the warehouse is right, the copy-out is the defect\n\nThe single-canonical-source concept is sound - Tools should exist as the source. But **every artifact that exists in N places will diverge; the drift observed is the steady state of copy-out, not a bug in execution.** The evidence in this repo already proves the failure is structural:\n\n- ASES crosslink-guard.ts is 42,140 bytes; the issue reports tripn 37.6K and Tools 33.5K - three divergent working copies of the same plugin, with the 'canonical' Tools copy the OLDEST. Canonicality was never enforced; the warehouse is a *place*, not a *mechanism*.\n- The section-5.5 two-repo sync rule (playbook) is a manual 'keep identical' procedure - and it ALREADY drifted: the durability-cadence amendment required #330/#331/#339 follow-up issues to force the mirror (playbook:314-317). A procedure cannot fix drift; it is drift's enabler.\n- The model whitelist: plugin.ts lives at ~/.config/opencode/plugins/ (user-level) and is the NEWEST (133L with #347 grok-ban) while Tools/plugins/plugin.ts (51L) is behind - because the artifact that exists in exactly ONE place (the live user-level dir) is the one that stayed current. That is direct evidence for single-copy distribution.\n\nA sync script + manifest is a *managed* version of copy-out. It will reduce silent drift but it does not remove divergence - it adds a new artifact (the manifest, the script) that must itself be maintained, generated, and checked in, or it will drift like everything else. **The copy/drift problem is inherent to copy-out; the answer is fewer copies, not better copying.**","created_at":"2026-08-14T23:52:04.661869142Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:prHqb5uo8bgYse0dKjeDZfRi7JuMFttOHgot8Aj7KZo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAghZRxLQOWt+gccT/3usNxuUm9XO7Mz+NXaeh1UiCXJG4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAKhipfqKxtL/G5nHCOMBIubjo7k00sWMABdVLQDkQ+bZGFO6qbaa7+i/vsY80GCGufICpFil7hnyMPCvx4ZcSDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:prHqb5uo8bgYse0dKjeDZfRi7JuMFttOHgot8Aj7KZo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAghZRxLQOWt+gccT/3usNxuUm9XO7Mz+NXaeh1UiCXJG4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOxw0/hEMuWViQizru3wZDNgjqFdteNTEaP8TYZEoy0u2ZblKLsG+iwvxialrAaSfDKFtNtwBsLYu2lA11bztAA="}
